windmill-lite reads openapi.yaml only in tests. The API-surface test in
../openapi_test.go checks that every operation the oracle client calls is
in it, and TestRouteTable in ../../platform/facade/routes_test.go generates
from it the facade's route table, ../../platform/facade/routes.json (each
operation's method, path template and operationId), which the facade
embeds as data. No code is generated from it.

Its references to ../../openflow.openapi.yaml are kept as Windmill wrote
them. They are relative to the file's place in Windmill's repository,
backend/windmill-api/openapi.yaml, where they name the OpenFlow schema at
the repository's root. From this directory they would name
internal/openflow.openapi.yaml, which does not exist, and nothing in
windmill-lite resolves them. That OpenFlow schema is vendored from the
same commit as ../../openflow/schema/openflow.openapi.yaml.
